description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/substrate-health-tick.ts. Two small contiguous string replacements in that ONE file. Do not change any other file.

EDIT 1 — add a minimum-sample threshold next to the two existing threshold reads. Replace this exact existing block:

  const confidenceFloor = pointer.confidence_floor ?? 10;
  const confidenceRatioThreshold = pointer.confidence_ratio_threshold ?? 0.25;

with:

  const confidenceFloor = pointer.confidence_floor ?? 10;
  const confidenceRatioThreshold = pointer.confidence_ratio_threshold ?? 0.25;
  // MINIMUM SAMPLE (2026-08-29). The ratio below is meaningless on a thin window: measured on the
  // same unchanged system 4h apart, total_pairs 17 with pairs_above_floor 2 gave 0.12 = FAIL, then
  // total_pairs 4 with the SAME numerator 2 gave 0.50 = PASS. The gate flipped because the
  // denominator collapsed, so an IDLE substrate manufactures lift. Below this many pairs the tick
  // has not measured confidence and must say so.
  const confidenceMinPairs = pointer.confidence_min_pairs ?? 8;

EDIT 2 — make the predicate return null (UNMEASURED) rather than a confident verdict on a thin sample. Replace this exact existing line:

    : (total_pairs === 0 ? false : pairs_above_floor / total_pairs >= confidenceRatioThreshold);

with:

    : (total_pairs < confidenceMinPairs ? null : pairs_above_floor / total_pairs >= confidenceRatioThreshold);

WHY null AND NOT false: this file already uses null for "couldn't measure this tick" three lines above, where !corpus_complete yields null, and its comment at 345-348 says a null dimension "makes overall_passing null ... which resets the lift streak honestly instead of falsely signalling a regression". A thin sample is owed the same honesty. Returning false would assert a measured regression, which is the opposite of the truth. Do NOT lower confidenceRatioThreshold instead.

The change must typecheck. VERIFY BY CONSEQUENCE: a reading of total_pairs=4 with pairs_above_floor=2 yields confidence_passing null and overall_passing null, where it currently yields true.

